From 4949296416617cf1ce8212e69d455b9b10e69806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:38:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: device capable integration drivers of the generic
 interface

The drivers of the `generic` interface (integration, initialize functions
and post-processings, for small strain, standard finite strain and finite
strain behaviours based on the Green-Lagrange or Hencky strains) are split
into:

- cores, which can be called in device code: the computation options are
  given explicitly (`ComputationOptions`) instead of being read in the `K`
  array, additional arguments are forwarded to the constructor of the
  behaviour, and exceptions are only caught on the host;
- the historical functions, with unchanged signatures, which decode the
  options and call the cores.

The `generic-parallel` interface will use the same cores. Fixes:

- the finite strain drivers tested the status with `if (r)`: the outputs
  were converted after a failure (`-1`) and not after an unreliable result
  (`0`), leaving the stress of the caller unchanged in this case;
- logarithmic strain, `DTAU_DDF` tangent operator: the spatial moduli at
  the end of the time step were computed with the logarithmic strain
  handler of the beginning of the time step;
- post-processings: the internal state variables at the end of the time
  step were not used, contrary to the documentation, and a null reference
  was passed when the initial state is not used;
- the initialize functions of the finite strain drivers based on the
  Green-Lagrange or Hencky strains did not compile (swapped arguments);
- the prediction operator ignored the request of the speed of sound when
  decoding the type of operator;
- the pointers of the behaviour data are restored if an initialize
  function throws.
---
